* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-lock (issue #37, Part of #16)
* PART A -- AS-DRAWN closed-loop PLL transient, transistor level.
* spec/porting-plan.md rows 7 (lock time), 10 (reference spur), 11 (power).
*
* `../testbench/run.sh` substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib section),
* @CORNER_RES@ (cornerRES.lib section), @TEMP@ (degC), @VDD@ (V), @FREF@
* (reference frequency, Hz), @TREF@/@TREFH@ (its period / high time, s),
* @IREF@ (charge-pump mirror reference current = the trim code, A),
* @B0V@/@B1V@ (VCO band-select code), @VC0@ (initial VCTRL), @TSTOP@,
* @TPRINT@ and @TMAX@ per ../corners/matrix.md.
*
* ===========================================================================
* TESTBENCH-LOCAL INTEGRATION -- THERE IS NO `pll_top` SCHEMATIC
* ===========================================================================
* `design/sg13cmos5l/` commits six blocks and no top level (see
* design/README.md). The block-to-block wiring below is therefore
* TESTBENCH-LOCAL: it is this deck's own reading of how the blocks are meant
* to connect, not a committed schematic. Every net it creates is named here
* so a reader can check it against the blocks' own pin lists:
*
*   ref  -> XPFD.REF          fb    -> XPFD.FB      (divider retimed output)
*   XPFD.UP/DN -> XCP.UP/DN and XLD.UP/DN
*   XCP.VOUT   -> vctrl (also XLF.VCTRL and XVCO.VCTRL)
*   XVCO.CLK   -> XDIV.CKIN and XDIV.CKIN_VCO
*   XDIV.FB    -> fb
*
* Each block sits on its OWN supply source (vdd_pfd / vdd_cp / vdd_vco /
* vdd_div / vdd_ld) so row 11 can measure every domain separately in ONE
* deck at ONE operating point, which is exactly what that row asks for.
* The supplies are ideal and all at @VDD@ -- this deck bounds domain
* currents, not supply-network IR drop.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TESTBENCH-LOCAL BIAS REPLICA -- NOT PART OF THE COMMITTED DESIGN
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Carried over verbatim (device sizes included) from
* ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/testbench/tb_cp_dc.sp.tmpl, for the same
* reason that record states: `cp.sch` exposes its cascode mirror gates as
* four pins and contains NO bias generator of its own. The replica runs off
* its own `vddrep` supply so that i(Vdd_cp) below is the charge pump's own
* current and NOT the replica's.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LUMPED MOM CAPS -- A HOST CONSTRAINT, STATED, NOT A DESIGN CHANGE
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* The installed PDK ships `cap_cmomi.osdi` / `cap_cmomf.osdi` as x86-64 ELF
* ONLY (verified with file(1) -- see ../records/RECORD-001 "Tooling note").
* This record was produced on an arm64 macOS host, where those two OSDI
* libraries cannot be dlopen'd at all, so no deck on this host can
* instantiate a `cap_cmomi`. `run.sh` therefore derives `loop_filter_tb.spice`
* and `lock_detector_tb.spice` from the FROZEN snapshots by replacing ONLY
* the `cap_cmomi` lines with ideal capacitors at the values
* ../../sg13cmos5l-loop-filter-momcap measured (and, for the two smaller
* instances, at that record's own measured area density). `XR1` stays the
* real `rppd` compact model. The snapshots themselves are never edited.
* ../records/RECORD-001 states what this substitution does and does not cost.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include pfd_snap.spice
.include cp_snap.spice
.include loop_filter_tb.spice
.include vco_tb.spice
.include divider_chain_snap.spice
.include lock_detector_tb.spice

Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

* --- per-domain supplies (row 11: one deck, one operating point) ---
Vdd_pfd vdd_pfd 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_cp  vdd_cp  0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_vco vdd_vco 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_div vdd_div 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_ld  vdd_ld  0 dc @VDD@
Vddrep  vddrep  0 dc @VDD@

* --- reference ---
Vref ref 0 pulse(0 @VDD@ 0 100p 100p @TREFH@ @TREF@)

* --- VCO band-select code (static) ---
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@

* --- divider modulus word P5..P0 = 000000 -> N = 2^6 = 64 (Vaucher chain) ---
Vp0 p0 0 dc 0
Vp1 p1 0 dc 0
Vp2 p2 0 dc 0
Vp3 p3 0 dc 0
Vp4 p4 0 dc 0
Vp5 p5 0 dc 0

* --- testbench-local cascode mirror reference for the charge pump ---
XMREFP1 nrp1 nbp  vddrep vddrep sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFP2 nbp  nbp  nrp1   vddrep sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefp nbp 0 dc @IREF@
XMREFN1 nrn1 nbn  0 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFN2 nbn  nbn  nrn1 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefn 0 nbn dc @IREF@

* --- the loop, block by block (real, unmodified subckts) ---
* .subckt pfd REF FB UP DN VDD VSS
XPFD ref fb up dn vdd_pfd 0 pfd
* .subckt cp UP DN IBP ICP IBN ICN VOUT VDD VSS
XCP up dn nbp nbp nbn nbn vctrl vdd_cp 0 cp
* .subckt loop_filter VCTRL VSS
XLF vctrl 0 loop_filter
* .subckt vco VCTRL B0 B1 CLK VDD_VCO GND_VCO
XVCO vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd_vco 0 vco
* .subckt divider_chain CKIN CKIN_VCO P0 P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 FB DIVOUT VDD_DIV VSS
XDIV clk clk p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 fb divout vdd_div 0 divider_chain
* .subckt lock_detector UP DN LOCK VDD VSS
XLD up dn lock vdd_ld 0 lock_detector

* Initial conditions. v(vctrl) is the stated starting control voltage (the
* filter has no DC path to ground -- ../../sg13cmos5l-loop-filter-momcap --
* so without this the node is undefined). v(xvco.ring1) is the same
* symmetry-breaking IC the Kvco and duty-cycle records use. The divider ICs
* put the Vaucher chain in a defined, legal state at t=0 (all cell outputs
* low, all modulus lines high); the chain has NO reset pin, which
* ../records/RECORD-001 records as a real design gap.
.ic v(vctrl)=@VC0@
.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5
.ic v(xdiv.ck1)=0 v(xdiv.ck2)=0 v(xdiv.ck3)=0 v(xdiv.ck4)=0 v(xdiv.ck5)=0
.ic v(divout)=0
.ic v(xdiv.mod0)=@VDD@ v(xdiv.mod1)=@VDD@ v(xdiv.mod2)=@VDD@
.ic v(xdiv.mod3)=@VDD@ v(xdiv.mod4)=@VDD@

.tran @TPRINT@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
meas tran i_pfd avg i(Vdd_pfd) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_cp  avg i(Vdd_cp)  from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_vco avg i(Vdd_vco) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_div avg i(Vdd_div) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_ld  avg i(Vdd_ld)  from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_avg avg v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_max max v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_min min v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
print i_pfd i_cp i_vco i_div i_ld vc_avg vc_max vc_min
* Uniformly-resampled waveform dump for the phase/frequency extractor in
* ../testbench/run.sh (the raw transient keeps ngspice's own non-uniform
* internal steps, which the extractor's edge interpolation does not want).
linearize v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk) v(lock)
wrdata wave.dat v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk) v(lock)
.endc
.end
